From be29bdfa097532fd5cbfcfce9051c63d00d310f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 16:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compact Library cards, add category/status filters, fix Cold Open blind spots

Library page:
- ProductCard's "Inside" skill row was hardcoded isRep ? RepSkillBadge :
  SquishySkillBadge — Cold Open skills silently rendered nothing (same
  bug class already fixed in workspace-home-client.tsx this session).
  Switched to the cross-product AnySkillBadge.
- Tightened card padding, icon size, and text sizes throughout (cards
  were larger than their content needed), and trimmed the page's own
  header/section spacing so the card grid starts higher instead of
  leaving open space above it.
- Added a Category filter (Setup / Monitoring / Outreach & Sequences /
  Analysis & Briefing / Crisis & Recovery, from the existing per-skill
  WORKER_CATEGORY_LIST) — a worker matches if any of its own skills
  falls in a selected category, since a single worker like Showtime
  spans several. Extended Status from All/Installed/Not installed with
  three more real, data-backed options: Needs configuration (installed,
  nothing enabled yet), Fully configured (every skill on), and Needs
  attention (success rate under 80%).

Two more spots had the same Cold-Open-invisible bug, both live and
both worse than a wrong icon:
- work-sidebar.tsx's installedProductIds filter only recognized
  "showtime"/"reputation-manager" — a Cold Open workspace's sidebar
  "Enabled Skills" grid always rendered completely empty.
- skills-nav-list.tsx's buildEntries() special-cased "showtime" and
  treated every other product as Reputation Manager — passing it Cold
  Open would have rendered Reputation Manager's skills a second time
  instead of Cold Open's own. Rebuilt on workersForProduct (the
  existing cross-product registry helper) and fixed toggleEndpoint to
  route to Cold Open's real toggle endpoint instead of assuming it's
  either the RM one or the generic Showtime one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
